  "body": "Closes #611\nClaim: mac/m4-captures\n\n**Problem.** HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-055 and §8 left these AQ create answers as *pending capture* (#611): a comment over the column length, a non-ASCII value, a non-numeric topic or post id, and an existing AQ id with a missing field. Without them the create of LOT-055 / LOT-134 would have to guess.\n\n**How it was captured.** Run 16 ran on a **local instance only**, set up as in #574: `roger21/toyo@96c0aea`, `aq/` unmodified, PHP 8.5.12, MariaDB 13.0.2, loopback address, the two tables of the published schema only, both clocks in UTC. Nothing was sent to the live service. It used the legacy body (UTF-8 bytes percent-encoded) with one field changed per state, and emptied the tables before each create, so the flood limit was never reached. The answer depends on the database's `sql_mode`, which is unknown for the live host, so I ran both modes.\n\n**What was captured** (`T72`-`T90`, `origin: local-instance`, fake values only):\n- **Strict (default) mode:** a comment of 1025 characters, a character outside the BMP in `nom` or `commentaire`, and a non-numeric or out-of-range id each get `-1`. A comment of exactly 1024 characters gets `1`.\n- **Empty `sql_mode`:** the same values get `1`. The database cuts the comment, stores the id as `0` and the emoji as `????` (`T90` lists it).\n- **Accents** are accepted and listed back unchanged (`T75`, `T76`).\n- **Addition to an existing AQ:** an empty `pseudo` gets `-3` (`T83`). Empty `nom`, `topic_id` and `topic_titre` are accepted (`T84`); the AQ keeps its own values (`T85`).\n\n**What changed.**\n- The captures, `corpus.json`, and `MANIFEST.md` (the Run 16 paragraph and 19 rows).\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-055 and §8: the facts are in, the *pending capture* marks are removed.\n- The LOT-055 spec and the kit README now point to the new captures.\n- `anonymize.py`: the AQ local check accepts this run's value forms and nothing else. The kit README asks for this (\"a new fake value form of a later run is added to `_V_AQ_LOCAL_*` with its test\").\n\n**Tests.**\n- `test_aq_own.AQLocalTests.test_the_611_forms_pass` checks that each form of the run passes. It failed on all ten forms before the change.\n- `test_the_611_forms_stay_closed` checks that nearby values still fail: 1023 `x`, 1025 `y`, another accent string, real-looking titles, `abcd`, an 11-digit id, a blank pseudo, and an empty pseudo with a non-alias comment.\n\n**Checks.**\n- Kit tests: 338 OK.\n- `check --corpus`: 606 of 606 clean.\n- `check --config` is clean.\n- `fold.py --check` is ok.\n- **Independent leak check passed**: a Sonnet sub-agent, independent of the redactor, found 0 hits for the DB password, the machine user, local paths, the credentials, the loopback address and its hashes, long hex strings and e-mail addresses.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
